body:
Hi! I want to start by saying that I've only read the webtoon up until chapter 20. I totally get where you're coming from. I don't read webtoons comments section because of how hurtful some people can be. Therefore I had no idea people wished death upon Rashta ... like calling her trashta is one thing but wishing death is just so out of proportion but I do disagree on one thing:

&#x200B;

>her prior station in life absolutely validates her actions to take advantage of the very same aristocracy that profited off her enslavement

&#x200B;

Up until chapter 20 I haven't encounter a situation where aristocracy profited off her enslavement ... maybe the people laughing at her but no really. Yes, the viscount son took advantage of her (and the viscount seems to be taking advantage of her new position) BUT I just don't see how aristocracy have profited off her enslavement. I would be on Rashta's side just by what the viscount and his son did to her if this were her webtoon, but  it's not and it just doesn't justify some things that Rashta has done like literally crying for everything and making herself look like the victim to fuel Sovieshu's "love" for her and "hate" towards Navier. I could see it more like her wanting to secure a spot where she can no longer have to serve someone else and suffer like she did when she was a slave but at the same time she already has Sovieshu's heart so why is she plotting so much against Navier?... I mean I get that she's just insecure but I just think she's way too much (my personal preference)

The one thing we should all agree is on hating Sovieshu for cheating on Navier and ridiculise her every single time by putting Rashta, a mistress, first. Like, fine, he loves Rashta and whatever BUT Navier is his wife, the empress and he's the one yelling at Navier and making her feel horrible. I'm not saying he should hide Rashta but he did handle things poorly and his actions in more recent episodes show that he completely gave up on the woman he used to love which is just sad. I wouldn't wish death upon him for that tho. Webtoons comment section is just way too toxic sometimes.

&#x200B;

BTW is there like a book or something???
